WEBVTT

00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:03.895
Preflight resilience begins with checking navigation status, home point,

00:00:03.895 --> 00:00:06.910
compass or heading consistency, maps, warnings, firmware state,

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:09.845
and expected flight modes according to approved procedures.

00:00:09.845 --> 00:00:12.720
An unexplained anomaly before launch is a reason to stop.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.040
Plan a simple route that can be understood visually.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:19.310
Maintain visual line of sight as required and appropriate, identify stable landmarks,

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:23.420
and avoid placing the aircraft where loss of automated position would immediately threaten

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:24.480
people or obstacles.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:28.560
Manual-control readiness means training for the aircraft's degraded behavior in authorized

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:29.370
safe conditions,

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:30.690
understanding mode changes,

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:33.820
and knowing the controls without improvisation during an incident.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:35.935
It does not mean experimenting with interference.

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:37.160
Use conservative automation.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:41.640
Verify each waypoint, route boundary, home point, return setting, and emergency area.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:46.690
Define abort criteria for navigation warnings, cue disagreement, drifting, mode changes,

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:49.200
unexpected route behavior, or low confidence.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:52.655
Identify landing areas along the mission, not only at the launch point.

00:00:52.655 --> 00:00:55.560
Consider wind, terrain, people, property, access, and battery.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:59.600
A nearby controlled landing may be safer than a long automated return through uncertain

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:00.530
navigation.

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:04.965
Document the plan, warnings, receiver status, visual references, settings, and crew roles.

00:01:04.965 --> 00:01:09.040
Resilience comes from independent cues, practiced decisions, and preserved margin,

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:12.430
not from assuming that more automation will overcome unreliable inputs.

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:16.800
Rehearse decisions through checklists and tabletop discussion using hypothetical warnings.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:20.530
Crews can practice communication, automation disengagement, landing selection,

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:24.320
and reporting without transmitting interference or creating risk to real navigation

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:24.960
systems.
